---
import { SitePage } from '@boombapbot/editor';
import Lettering from '../components/Lettering.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="Docs · boombapbot"
  description="How to use РИТМ-12, the boombapbot drum machine: writing patterns, accents, recording by tapping, swing, the sound knobs, the effect and exporting."
>
  <SitePage client:load baseUrl={base} current="docs">
    <h1>How to use РИТМ-12</h1>
    <p class="sb-lede">
      Press the play key and it plays. Everything else on the panel changes what it plays or how it sounds. The
      lettering is Russian, so this page gives each control as it is lettered and says what it is.
    </p>

    <Section title="The idea">
      <p>
        The machine remembers four <strong>patterns</strong>: А, Б, В and Г. A pattern is one measure of sixteen
        steps. It has a row for each of the eight instruments and one row of accents, and each step in a row is on
        or off.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Writing a pattern">
      <ol>
        <li>Press the play key, the first of the three under <Lettering>УПРАВЛЕНИЕ</Lettering>. The pattern goes round.</li>
        <li>
          Press an instrument key on the left, under <Lettering>ИНСТРУМЕНТЫ</Lettering>. It plays the sound and selects
          it, and its lamp stays lit.
        </li>
        <li>
          Press the step keys, the row of sixteen under <Lettering>СЕКВЕНСЕР</Lettering>, where it should play. A lit
          key is a step that is on; press it again to turn it off.
        </li>
        <li>Choose another instrument and carry on. The step keys always show the instrument that is selected.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>The instruments</h3>
      <dl>
        <dt><Lettering>БАС</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>Kick.</dd>
        <dt><Lettering>МАЛЫЙ</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>Snare.</dd>
        <dt><Lettering>ХЛОП</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>Clap.</dd>
        <dt><Lettering>ХЭТ З</Lettering> and <Lettering>ХЭТ О</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>Closed hat and open hat. Each one cuts the other off.</dd>
        <dt><Lettering>ТОМ</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>Tom.</dd>
        <dt><Lettering>РИМ</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>Rim.</dd>
        <dt><Lettering>ПЕРК</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>Percussion.</dd>
      </dl>

      <h3>Accents</h3>
      <p>
        The <Lettering>РЕЖИМ ЗАПИСИ</Lettering> switch decides what the step keys write. On <Lettering>УДАРЫ</Lettering> they
        write hits of the selected instrument. On <Lettering>АКЦЕНТЫ</Lettering> they write the pattern's accents. Every
        instrument that plays on an accented step is louder, by as much as the <Lettering>АКЦЕНТ</Lettering> knob says.
      </p>

      <h3>Recording by tapping</h3>
      <p>
        Press the record key, the one with the red dot, while the pattern plays. Now each instrument key you
        press in time is written on the step it lands on. Press record again to stop. Everything tapped in one go
        is one undo step.
      </p>

      <h3>Mute, dice and clear</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Lettering>МУТ</Lettering> silences the selected instrument and leaves its steps where they are.</li>
        <li>The key with the die writes a new row for the selected instrument, by chance.</li>
        <li><Lettering>СБРОС</Lettering> empties the pattern you are on. Undo brings it back.</li>
      </ul>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Patterns, measure and tempo">
      <dl>
        <dt><Lettering>ПАТТЕРН</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>
          The keys А, Б, В and Г choose the pattern you see and hear. Pressed while the machine plays, the new one
          takes over at the end of the measure.
        </dd>
        <dt><Lettering>РАЗМЕР</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>
          The length of a measure, for all four patterns. <strong>16</strong> is sixteen steps, four to the
          beat. <strong>12</strong> is twelve steps of triplets, three to the beat, and the last four step keys sit
          out.
        </dd>
        <dt><Lettering>ТЕМП</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>From 40 to 300 beats a minute. The screen shows the number.</dd>
        <dt><Lettering>СВИНГ</Lettering></dt>
        <dd>Plays every second step late, from not at all up to a hard shuffle. Triplets do not swing.</dd>
      </dl>
    </Section>

    <Section title="The sounds">
      <ul>
        <li>The knob beside each instrument key is that instrument's level.</li>
        <li>
          The three knobs under <Lettering>ОБРАБОТКА ГОЛОСА</Lettering> work on the selected
          instrument: <Lettering>ПИТЧ</Lettering> is its pitch, <Lettering>ЗАТУХАНИЕ</Lettering> how long it rings,
          and <Lettering>ТОН</Lettering> how bright it is. Each instrument keeps its own settings.
        </li>
        <li><Lettering>ГРОМКОСТЬ</Lettering> is the volume of the whole machine, and the <Lettering>УРОВЕНЬ</Lettering> meter shows how loud it is.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Drag a knob up or down to turn it, or focus it and use the arrow keys. The screen says what the control
        you just touched did.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="The effect">
      <p>
        There is one effect on the whole machine. Press the <Lettering>ЭФФЕКТ</Lettering> selector to step to the next
        of four: <Lettering>ДИЛЭЙ</Lettering> is an echo, <Lettering>РЕВЕРБ</Lettering> a reverb, <Lettering>ФЛЭНЖЕР</Lettering> a
        flanger and <Lettering>ХОР</Lettering> a chorus. The <Lettering>СМЕСЬ</Lettering> knob sets how much of it you hear.
        At 0 there is none.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Keeping what you make">
      <p>
        Everything is saved in this browser as you go. The cog in the footer opens settings, where you can name
        your beat, undo and redo, put the starter patterns back, clear one pattern or everything, and import or
        export. With a free account you can also save up to 20 beats to it from the account button in the footer,
        and load them on another device.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Project file</strong> holds everything the machine remembers, and opens here again.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>WAV and MIDI</strong> hold the pattern you are on, as a loop of one measure. The WAV has the
          effect in it.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Section>

    <Section title="What comes with it">
      <p>A new machine has a beat on А and a busier turn of it on Б. В and Г are empty.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Beats from the earlier machine">
      <p>
        boombapbot used to be a different machine. A beat made on it opens here as a РИТМ-12 beat, whether it is
        the draft in this browser, a project file or a beat saved to your account. The rhythm that machine was on
        becomes pattern А, and a notice lists what did not fit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing old is written over. The earlier draft stays in this browser, and a beat in your account stays as
        it was: saving the one that opened here adds a new beat beside it.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="On a phone">
      <p>
        A phone gets the same machine laid out as a column: the screen, the eight instruments, the step keys in two
        rows, and the transport. The knobs are behind three tabs. <Lettering>ГОЛОС</Lettering> has the selected
        instrument's pitch, decay, tone and level, <Lettering>ТЕМП</Lettering> has tempo, swing, accent and the
        measure, and <Lettering>ЭФФЕКТ</Lettering> has the effect, its mix and the volume. A tablet held upright
        gets it too, a little larger.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is the same beat either way. To see the picture on a small screen, add <code>?panel=picture</code> to
        the address: it scrolls sideways, or fits the screen at the press of <strong>Fit to screen</strong>.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Keyboard">
      <dl>
        <dt><kbd>Space</kbd></dt>
        <dd>Start or stop.</dd>
        <dt>Arrow keys</dt>
        <dd>Move between step keys, and turn the knob that has focus.</dd>
        <dt><kbd>Enter</kbd></dt>
        <dd>Press the key that has focus.</dd>
        <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt>
        <dd>Close a window.</dd>
        <dt><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> or <kbd>Cmd</kbd> + <kbd>Z</kbd></dt>
        <dd>Undo. Add <kbd>Shift</kbd> to redo.</dd>
      </dl>
    </Section>

    <Section title="The power switch">
      <p>
        <Lettering>СЕТЬ</Lettering> turns the machine off: it goes dark, it stops, and nothing else on it answers until
        you switch it back on. Nothing it remembers is lost.
      </p>
    </Section>
  </SitePage>
</Base>
